    <article class="poster" id="p-thesis-spam" data-poster-panel="p-thesis-spam" hidden aria-label="Poster: Detecting Online Gambling Spam Comments on YouTube">
      <header class="poster__head">
        <div class="poster__id">
          <h3 class="poster__title">Undergraduate Thesis: Detecting Online Gambling Spam Comments on YouTube</h3>
          <p class="poster__sub">ITENAS — Undergraduate Thesis · Bandung, ID · Nov 2025 – June 2026</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="poster__cols">
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4>
          <p>
            How do Indonesian character obfuscations, emoji padding, and intentional spelling variations degrade spam classifiers, and can a hybrid representation of 1,000 TF-IDF character trigrams + 9 statistical features restore 99.56% detection precision?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4>
          <ul class="poster__list">
            <li>Evaluated adversarial Indonesian spam comments promoting online gambling on YouTube, characterized by intentional character swapping, emoji padding, and zero-width spaces.</li>
            <li>Engineered a hybrid feature representation combining 1,000 TF-IDF character trigram features with 9 domain-specific numerical statistical indicators.</li>
            <li>Tuned Random Forest classifier using GridSearchCV and evaluated across rigorous 10-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation.</li>
            <li>Achieved 99.56% across Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-Score, earning highest defense honors from the Informatics Faculty Examination Board.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4>
        <p>
          Demonstrates that lightweight character n-gram statistical modeling significantly outperforms heavy LLMs in latency and compute efficiency for real-time Indonesian comment filtering.
        </p>
      </div>

